(1414338, 181519, 25655, '<td valign="top">I love the warm tones in this photo.<br/>the special shape of the glass also adds a lot to the interest.<br/>The focus and the lights reflections are also very pleasing to the viewer.<br/>The only thing that I find a little distracting is the bottom area of the photo. It looks a little bit too busy to me.<br/>I think that a cleaner look in that area, with maybe just a tiny bit of melting water under the cube that is right of center, would be better.<br/>Also, I am not sure how many of the people here will think of ice cubes as granular. I really hope I am wrong about this, but some of the people might consider this as not exactly meeting the challenge.<br/>Anyway, I like the theme a lot! <br/></td>', 'I love the warm tones in this photo.the special shape of the glass also adds a lot to the interest.The focus and the lights reflections are also very pleasing to the viewer.The only thing that I find a little distracting is the bottom area of the photo. It looks a little bit too busy to me.I think that a cleaner look in that area, with maybe just a tiny bit of melting water under the cube that is right of center, would be better.Also, I am not sure how many of the people here will think of ice cubes as granular. I really hope I am wrong about this, but some of the people might consider this as not exactly meeting the challenge.Anyway, I like the theme a lot! ', '2005-05-26 17:37:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(1414339, 181531, 35602, '<td valign="top">The face seems either overexposed or overprocessed.  Perhaps you were color correcting.  The concept was very good, though.</td>', 'The face seems either overexposed or overprocessed.  Perhaps you were color correcting.  The concept was very good, though.', '2005-05-26 17:38:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1414340, 181526, 32848, '<td valign="top">Nice texture and focus.</td>', 'Nice texture and focus.', '2005-05-26 17:39:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(1414345, 179852, 35602, '<td valign="top">Love your title.  The one thing you might have done is have the dust more in the light.  Just turning the bowl would have reconfigured the shot and placed the light on the dust.  You might have also tried to lock your focus on the cereal.  I think the camera focused more on the placemat.</td>', 'Love your title.  The one thing you might have done is have the dust more in the light.  Just turning the bowl would have reconfigured the shot and placed the light on the dust.  You might have also tried to lock your focus on the cereal.  I think the camera focused more on the placemat.', '2005-05-26 17:44:38.000000', NULL, 1),
