(1425650, 181621, 19010, '<td valign="top">Greetings From the Gritique Club!!!<br/> <br/>Initial Impact: ooh a flower...<br/> <br/>Lighting: The lighting on this one is simple yet well done. You have no distracting shadows and you don''t look to have any blown out highlights.<br/> <br/>Color: The browns are very rich and enjoyable. I Especialy like the way the green fades out and slowley disapears from the center in a smooth transition. <br/> <br/>Focus: Very crisp image with a nice DOF. I enjoy the details that you captured on the pistle and the granual pollen that has fallen off to the sides.<br/> <br/>Composition: I am happy with the composition of the image. Every thing looks to be proportional. However due to the stagering number of macro flowers I would suggest shooting this fro somthing other than a head on angle. Try shooting it from the side a bit or perhaps using dry ice to produce some smoke on the interior.<br/> <br/>Overall: other that the fact that the shot is a very common one this is a very nice shot. I feel that any flower shot would hae trouble getting a high placing without havingsomthing special to help it stand out fronm the crowd. But as is it looks like your stock "not to be mistaken with bad" photo. I feel that this is a good image but lacked the wow! factor required to bring this up with the higher rating shots.<br/> <br/>Tristalisk</td>', 'Greetings From the Gritique Club!!! Initial Impact: ooh a flower... Lighting: The lighting on this one is simple yet well done. You have no distracting shadows and you don''t look to have any blown out highlights. Color: The browns are very rich and enjoyable. I Especialy like the way the green fades out and slowley disapears from the center in a smooth transition.  Focus: Very crisp image with a nice DOF. I enjoy the details that you captured on the pistle and the granual pollen that has fallen off to the sides. Composition: I am happy with the composition of the image. Every thing looks to be proportional. However due to the stagering number of macro flowers I would suggest shooting this fro somthing other than a head on angle. Try shooting it from the side a bit or perhaps using dry ice to produce some smoke on the interior. Overall: other that the fact that the shot is a very common one this is a very nice shot. I feel that any flower shot would hae trouble getting a high placing without havingsomthing special to help it stand out fronm the crowd. But as is it looks like your stock "not to be mistaken with bad" photo. I feel that this is a good image but lacked the wow! factor required to bring this up with the higher rating shots. Tristalisk', '2005-06-01 09:47:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(1425676, 180733, 24495, '<td valign="top">Looks like ''Salt of Time''!</td>', 'Looks like ''Salt of Time''!', '2005-06-01 09:59:03.000000', NULL, 0),
