(1429813, 180306, 33982, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by lbWhaples:</b></div><hr/><i> So did you have to refill the cone after every shot? </i></td></tr></table> <br/>no -- it would take a few min. to throw it around &amp; some times  i just emptied it to try a new color or etc .. <br/> <br/>what was also really neat -- just leaving a bit-o-dust and the speaker on  a more normal volume -- allowed the dust to ''creep'' along .. which was facinating to watch but would make for a boring still image // <br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by lbWhaples: So did you have to refill the cone after every shot?  no -- it would take a few min. to throw it around & some times  i just emptied it to try a new color or etc ..  what was also really neat -- just leaving a bit-o-dust and the speaker on  a more normal volume -- allowed the dust to ''creep'' along .. which was facinating to watch but would make for a boring still image //  ', '2005-06-02 18:08:50.000000', NULL, 0),
